{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Deep pit, folly</b> — two joined together." "<b>Deep pit</b> — on the pattern of גולה (exile). And the meaning: as a שוחה (pit) is deep, so the mouth of strange women is [deep] for those doomed — whomever HaShem has doomed and desires his death will fall there. But the youth, even though folly is bound in his heart, it is fitting to strike him with the rod of discipline, for it will distance the folly from him."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:12.286192544Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}